# GoDaddy DNS-01 credentials for certbot-dns-godaddy.
#
# How to generate (2026-04 GoDaddy UI; subject to change):
#   1. Sign in at https://godaddy.com with the account that owns the domain.
#   2. Visit https://developer.godaddy.com/keys (direct link) or navigate:
#        profile menu → "API keys" or https://account.godaddy.com → Developer Portal.
#   3. Click "Create New API Key".
#   4. Name: "certbot-dns-godaddy-deepaksharma-live" (or similar).
#   5. Environment: **Production** (NOT "OTE" — OTE keys do not affect the
#      live zone; certbot would succeed against OTE but no DNS records would
#      ever appear in your real zone).
#   6. Copy the **Key** and **Secret** into this file below.
#   7. Save this file as `godaddy.ini` (drop the `.example` suffix).
#   8. `chmod 600 certbot/secrets/godaddy.ini`
#
# GoDaddy API limitation (verified 2026-04): accounts with fewer than 10
# registered domains OR on the free / Basic plan receive HTTP 403
# "UNABLE_TO_AUTHENTICATE" when calling the DNS API, even with a valid key.
# If issue-cert.sh --provider=godaddy fails with that error, the API is not
# accessible for this account — fall back to:
#   (a) manual DNS-01   (certbot/issue-cert-manual.sh)        — no auto-renew
#   (b) DNS delegation  (docs/GODADDY_DNS_SETUP.md Path A)    — auto-renew, recommended
# See docs/GODADDY_DNS_SETUP.md for end-to-end options.
#
# SECURITY:
#   * NEVER commit this file after you fill it in. certbot/secrets/.gitignore
#     denies *.ini / *.env by default — verify before pushing.
#   * If this leaks, revoke immediately at https://developer.godaddy.com/keys
#     and regenerate. Keys do not auto-rotate.
#   * Scope: GoDaddy API keys are unfortunately account-global; they cannot be
#     scoped to a single domain. Treat them as sensitive as a full account
#     password.

dns_godaddy_secret = REPLACE_WITH_GODADDY_API_SECRET
dns_godaddy_key    = REPLACE_WITH_GODADDY_API_KEY
